MmsService: carry MMS through the WSA-Next host when Android has no cellular network.

On Windows Subsystem for Android the SIM is in the PC's modem, which Windows drives; Android
gets SMS through the RIL bridge but has no mobile data network, so MMS could not be sent or
downloaded. When the WSA-Next relay daemon is present (/dev/socket/wsa_mms), MmsService asks
no cellular network: each HTTP exchange goes through a loopback tunnel to the daemon, and
WSA-Next on Windows opens the APN on the modem (ConnectivityManager.AcquireConnectionAsync)
and connects to the APN's MMS proxy or MMS server. ApnSettings keeps the APN name and
credentials for that; the "MMS data enabled" check is skipped, since Android has no mobile
data setting there.

